{
  "text": " The third thing the tarn tried was their catcher. He was a small fair boy with a fresh bandage on his wrist, and he came in low on the north side with his ward up at his hip, small the width of a doormat, and set it under the litter's middle. It was clever. He meant to lift the litter's middle on his tray and walk it back east over the line while Kiva sat on the head. A ward lifts. That is what a catcher's tray is for.",
